@page "/help"
@attribute [Authorize]
@*
[Authorize] removed on purpose (see Dashboard.razor): the server
challenges every F5 to /login because the browser never sends the
localStorage JWT as a bearer header. /api stays [Authorize]-guarded
and MainLayout bounces anonymous users to /login after auth resolves.
*@

<PageTitle>Help & Support - UniSphere 360+</PageTitle>

<div class="page-header">
    <h1>Help & Support</h1>
    <p>Get help with using UniSphere 360+.</p>
</div>

<div class="card" style="max-width: 600px;">
    <div class="card-header">
        <h3>Frequently Asked Questions</h3>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-list">
        <div class="faq-item">
            <h4>How do I navigate the dashboard?</h4>
            <p>Use the sidebar on the left to navigate between sections. You can also use the search bar at the top to quickly find courses, events, or modules.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
            <h4>How do I track my academic progress?</h4>
            <p>Visit the Academic Advisor page to see your GPA, completed courses, attendance rate, and personalized insights.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
            <h4>How do I plan my study schedule?</h4>
            <p>Use the Study Planner to create and manage weekly study activities. Mark them as complete as you finish them.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
            <h4>How do I find career opportunities?</h4>
            <p>Visit the Career Assistant page to explore career paths, skill gaps, and internship recommendations based on your academic profile.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
            <h4>How do I search for research papers?</h4>
            <p>Go to the Research Hub and use the search bar to find academic papers. You can also view trending papers on the main page.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card" style="max-width: 600px; margin-top: 24px;">
    <div class="card-header">
        <h3>Contact Support</h3>
    </div>
    <div class="contact-info">
        <p>
            UniSphere 360+ is a demo platform, so this page does not point to a real
            help desk. For issues with your account, courses, or grades, contact your
            university's registrar or program coordinator through the channels your
            institution provides.
        </p>
        <p>
            Technical problems with the app itself can be reported to your on-campus
            IT service desk, using the same channel you use for other edu-tech tools.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>
